      <div class="case-content">
        <section id="summary">
          <h2>1. Offloading heavy compute from the UI isolate</h2>
          <p>
            Running large spreadsheet recalculations, real-time 3D geometry projection, SIMD media transforms, or local NLU inference on a Flutter/Dart UI isolate degrades frame pacing, while exposing raw heap pointers over FFI introduces use-after-free, double-free, and undefined behavior when Rust panics unwind across C frames.
          </p>
          <p>
            Meson isolates <strong>49 native Rust APIs</strong> across <strong>8 workspace crates</strong> (50,270 LOC) behind the zero-dependency generational arena pattern open-sourced in <code>ffi-arena-bridge</code>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="ffi">
          <h2>2. Generational FFI arenas (<code>ffi-arena-bridge</code>) &amp; panic shields</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Opaque <code>u64</code> handles instead of raw pointers (<code>abi.rs</code>, <code>engine.rs</code>):</strong> <code>ArenaBridge</code> packs slot index + <code>GenerationId</code> into a 64-bit <code>OpaqueHandle</code>. Stale reads or double-frees fail generation checks and return deterministic error codes instead of corrupting memory.</li>
            <li><strong>Mandatory <code>catch_unwind</code> boundary:</strong> every <code>extern "C"</code> entry point traps Rust panics and translates them into structured error codes.</li>
            <li><strong>Bounded slice views &amp; trigram search (<code>trigram.rs</code>):</strong> <code>SafeSliceView</code> enforces explicit buffer bounds alongside a deterministic trigram catalog verified by <code>tests/integration_ffi.rs</code> and the live C99 <code>cdylib</code> binary <code>tests/c_smoke.c</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="dag">
          <h2>3. Native Office suite: <code>ChunkedColumn</code> (1M rows), DAG &amp; OOXML roundtrip</h2>
          <p>
            <code>crates/meson_tools</code> (19 files · 3,407 LOC · <strong>21/21 passing tests</strong>) delivers native desktop productivity engines with zero Office runtime dependencies:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Sparse bit-masked columnar storage (<code>chunked_store.rs</code>):</strong> partitions columns into fixed blocks of <code>CHUNK_SIZE = 16,384</code> rows addressed via bit shifts (<code>row &gt;&gt; 14</code>, mask <code>0x3FFF</code>) with a parallel <code>numeric_cache: Vec&lt;Vec&lt;Option&lt;f64&gt;&gt;&gt;</code> so aggregate stats (<code>count</code>, <code>sum</code>, <code>avg</code>, <code>min</code>, <code>max</code>) skip hot-path string parsing; verified by <code>test_chunked_million_row_stats</code> and <code>test_chunked_streaming_csv</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Incremental DAG dependency solver (<code>dependency_graph.rs</code>, <code>parser.rs</code>, <code>evaluator.rs</code>):</strong> rejects circular references before propagation and topologically re-evaluates only affected downstream cells (<code>SUMIF</code>, <code>COUNTIF</code>, <code>VLOOKUP</code>, <code>IF</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>Pure-Rust OOXML roundtrips:</strong> <code>xlsx.rs</code> (345 LOC, <code>sharedStrings.xml</code> + <code>ZipWriter</code>), <code>writer_engine.rs</code> (489 LOC, <code>.docx</code>), and <code>slides_engine.rs</code> (261 LOC, <code>.pptx</code>), verified via <code>test_xlsx_export_and_import_roundtrip</code>, <code>test_generate_docx_bytes</code>, and <code>test_pptx_generate_and_parse_roundtrip</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="spatial">
          <h2>4. Rust isometric 3D projection &amp; Flame 2.5D spatial layout engine</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Isometric 3D micro-renderer (<code>api/procedural_3d_engine.rs</code>, 335 LOC):</strong> invoked synchronously over <code>#[frb(sync)]</code> (<code>process_3d_render</code>), performs X/Y rotation on boxes and prisms, per-face ARGB brightness shading, exact isometric projection (<code>cos 30° = 0.8660254</code>, <code>sin 30° = 0.5</code>), and painter's depth sorting to add 3D volume directly atop Flame's 2D canvas without embedding a heavy 3D engine.</li>
            <li><strong>Collision, magnetic snapping &amp; layout diffing (<code>table_layout_engine.rs</code>, 485 LOC):</strong> provides grid snapping (<code>snap_to_grid</code>), AABB collision checks (<code>check_collision</code>), 10-alignment magnetic floor-block snapping (<code>snap_floor_block</code>), and minimal upsert/delete diffing (<code>compute_layout_diff</code>), powering both the <code>meson_business</code> floor editor and visual table selection inside <code>meson_customer</code> (backed by 20+ Dart test files under <code>test/features/tables/</code>).</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="native">
          <h2>5. Delta patching (<code>qbsdiff</code>), SIMD, Edge AI (Paper 15) &amp; <code>meson_gpui</code></h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Binary delta updates (<code>crates/meson_shell</code> · 5/5 tests):</strong> <code>meson_updater</code> and <code>meson_patcher</code> apply <code>qbsdiff</code> binary patches with download verification and staged rollout (<code>test_delta_diffing_and_patching</code>, <code>test_apply_delta_update_staged</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>SIMD media &amp; Edge AI/Voice:</strong> <code>meson_media</code> accelerates image resizing via <code>fast_image_resize</code>; <code>crates/meson_speech_worker</code> (472 LOC, <code>whisper-rs</code>) provides local STT, while the full NLU engine (<code>crates/meson_ai</code>, 16,006 LOC, 300/300 tests) and Flutter UI automation engine are documented in <a href="/en/lab/meson-edge-nlu-automation/">Paper 15</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Pure-Rust GPUI desktop exploration (<code>meson_gpui</code>):</strong> <strong>15 Rust files (2,922 LOC)</strong> on <code>gpui 0.2.2</code> (<code>desktop_grid.rs</code>, <code>taskbar.rs</code>, <code>window_layer.rs</code>, <code>widgets_panel.rs</code>) — corrected from v1.0 — validate direct GPU-rendered desktop shells without WebViews or Dart runtimes.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="validity">
          <h2>6. Live CI / <code>cargo test</code> verification &amp; limits</h2>
          <p>
            <a href="https://github.com/M4QSZ/ffi-arena-bridge" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ffi-arena-bridge</a> runs Rust integration tests and compiles/executes a live C99 consumer against the shared library in GitHub Actions (Ubuntu and Windows). In Meson's private workspace, a live November 2026 execution of <code>cargo test -p meson_ai -p meson_features -p meson_tools -p meson_shell</code> passed <strong>404 / 404 tests (0 failures)</strong>: 300 in <code>meson_ai</code>, 78 in <code>meson_features</code>, 21 in <code>meson_tools</code>, and 5 in <code>meson_shell</code>.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Limits:</strong> reproducible public micro-benchmarks for 1M FFI crossings and p95 <code>process_3d_render</code> timings on low-end Android devices remain future work.
          </p>
        </section>
